# Clerk Auth & Data Ownership

All authentication is handled by Clerk. Every server-side data access **must** be scoped to the authenticated user. Never return, modify, or delete data that belongs to another user.

## Get the current user

```typescript
import { auth } from '@clerk/nextjs/server';
import { redirect } from 'next/navigation';

const { userId } = await auth();
if (!userId) redirect('/'); // no dedicated sign-in page — homepage has sign-in/sign-up buttons
```

## Querying decks

`decks` rows carry a `clerkUserId` column. Always filter by it.

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD
const userDecks = await db.select().from(decks).where(eq(decks.clerkUserId, userId));

// ❌ BAD — returns every user's decks
const allDecks = await db.select().from(decks);
```

## Querying cards

`cards` have no direct `clerkUserId`; they belong to a deck. Verify deck ownership before accessing cards.

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD — join through the owned deck
const userCards = await db
  .select({ card: cards })
  .from(cards)
  .innerJoin(decks, eq(cards.deckId, decks.id))
  .where(and(eq(decks.clerkUserId, userId), eq(decks.id, deckId)));

// ❌ BAD — fetches cards without verifying ownership
const allCards = await db.select().from(cards).where(eq(cards.deckId, deckId));
```

## Mutations (update / delete)

Always scope writes to the authenticated user. For `cards`, join through `decks`.

```typescript
// ✅ Update a deck — only if it belongs to the user
await db.update(decks).set({ name }).where(and(eq(decks.id, deckId), eq(decks.clerkUserId, userId)));

// ✅ Delete a card — verify parent deck ownership first
const [ownerDeck] = await db.select().from(decks).where(and(eq(decks.id, deckId), eq(decks.clerkUserId, userId)));
if (!ownerDeck) throw new Error('Forbidden');
await db.delete(cards).where(eq(cards.id, cardId));
```

## Rules

- Call `auth()` at the top of every Server Action and Route Handler.
- Redirect to `/` (homepage) before touching the database if `userId` is null. The homepage is where sign-in/sign-up buttons live — there is no dedicated `/sign-in` page.
- Never trust client-supplied IDs alone — always cross-check against `clerkUserId`.
- Never expose raw database rows in responses without first verifying ownership.
